-- Consistency check after a pass through the concept layer. Binds $p (the packet), $model (the rule model the
-- profile was written from) and $profile ({part: text}). Reports whether MET and NOT MET overlap or leave a gap,
-- and classifies every model node without a packet source as an ADDITION (the packet is silent on it) or a
-- CONTRADICTION (the packet says otherwise, with the passage quoted). Warns; never edits.
$json%($parse%(=>("You check an evaluation profile and the rule model it was written from against the rule's packet.\n\n1. MET and NOT MET must not overlap: is there a concrete case that satisfies both as written? And among cases where the rule applies, is there a case neither covers (and UNCERTAIN does not)?\n2. For each node of the RULE MODEL whose source is empty or says it is not in the packet, decide: \"addition\" if the packet is silent on it (it adds an exception, condition or fact the packet neither states nor rules out), or \"contradiction\" if the packet says otherwise (quote the passage).\n\nReply with JSON only: {\"overlap\": true | false, \"overlap_case\": \"<a case, or empty>\", \"gap\": true | false, \"gap_case\": \"<a case, or empty>\", \"nodes\": [{\"id\": \"<node id>\", \"kind\": \"addition\" | \"contradiction\", \"passage\": \"<the packet passage it contradicts, or empty>\"}]}\n\nPACKET:\n" ++ $json%$p ++ "\n\nRULE MODEL:\n" ++ $json%$model ++ "\n\nPROFILE:\n" ++ $json%$profile)))
